---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import chairman from "../assets/photos/chairman.jpg";
import founder from "../assets/photos/vasantrao.jpg";
---

<Base
  title="Leadership"
  description="Shrinivas V. Dempo, chairman of the Dempo Group, with the family line and the other people named on dempos.com. No officers have been added."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split uneven">
      <figure class="figure portrait" data-reveal>
        <Image
          src={chairman}
          alt="Shrinivas V. Dempo, chairman of the Dempo Group."
          widths={[480, 800]}
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 420px, 100vw"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Shrinivas V. Dempo. Image credit on the profile page: The Art of Blinks / Incredible Goa.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">Chairman</span>
        <h1 class="h-display-md">Shrinivas V. Dempo</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Chairman of the Goa-based Dempo Group of Companies. Born in Mumbai into a Goan
          family the homepage describes as having five and a half centuries of business
          and social responsibility behind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The profile lists diversified interests in calcined petroleum coke, shipbuilding,
          food processing, real estate and newspaper publishing. He has chaired the western
          region of the Confederation of Indian Industry and is immediate past president of
          AIMA. On 1 July 2023 he was elected president of the Goa Chamber of Commerce and
          Industry. In 2013 he was named honorary vice consul of Italy in Goa. He was
          appointed chairman, as an independent director, of Automobile Corporation of Goa,
          a Tata Group company, and on 25 May 2021 additional director of Kirloskar Brothers Limited.
        </p>
        <p>
          He earned bachelor’s and master’s degrees from the University of Mumbai in 1990
          and 1992, and a Master of Science in Industrial Administration and Finance from
          Carnegie Mellon University in 1995. In 2019 he joined that university’s Board of
          Trustees. In 2020 he received the Tepper Achievement Award. With Pallavi S. Dempo
          he has supported the Tepper Quad Building on the David A. Tepper Quadrangle, after
          endowing a chair in his grandfather’s name dedicated to the inclusive growth of India.
        </p>
        <p>
          In football, he was named among the 50 most influential people in Indian sports
          in the 2010 Sports Illustrated Power list. He was Goa venue director for the FIFA
          U-17 World Cup in 2017, president of the Goa Football Association from October 2010
          to July 2014, and AIFF vice president from December 2012 to December 2016.
        </p>
        <p>
          He sits on the Executive Council of Goa University, is associated with the Charles
          Correa Foundation, and is president of the Goa Cancer Society. In 2014 Enterprise
          Asia gave him the Asia Pacific Outstanding Entrepreneurship Award India.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.dempos.com/about-us/chairmans-profile/">Chairman’s profile</a>
          ·
          <a href="https://www.dempos.com/about-us/chairmans-address/">Chairman’s address</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">From the address</span>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="color: white; max-width: 22ch">
        “Let me invite and welcome you to join in on this journey of discovery.”
        <footer style="color: #c4bfb6">Shrinivas V. Dempo, chairman’s address</footer>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 2rem">
        <p>
          The address presents the site as an interface between society and the House of
          Dempo, and describes businesses and not-for-profits as steps in nation-building.
          It lists vessels, newspapers, a football team, baby foods, chemicals and a travel
          agency among the things the Group does. Social programmes, it says, aim at higher
          education, sporting excellence, cultural initiatives, environmental conservation,
          affirmative action, and cleanliness and sanitation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Speaking in 2025 at Dempo House, when the Group supported para-footballer Niklesh
          Pednekar, he said: “Let what has happened remain in the past, don’t let it take
          away from your future.”
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Named on the site</span>
      <h2 class="quote" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem">The line, and the people the pages actually name.</h2>
      <div class="split">
        <figure class="figure">
          <Image
            src={founder}
            alt="Vasantrao S. Dempo, founder chairman of the Dempo Group."
            widths={[400, 700]}
            sizes="(min-width: 800px) 40vw, 100vw"
          />
          <figcaption>Vasantrao S. Dempo, Padma Shri, 1991.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="rule-list">
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Founder</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Vasantrao S. Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Founder chairman. Padma Shri in 1991 for trade and industry. The Kalpavriksha
              portrait calls him entrepreneur, statesman and philanthropist. Memorial essays
              dated 2000 refer to him as the late founder. His year of birth is not settled
              on the site. [Placeholder: client to confirm]
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Co-founder</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Vaikunthrao S. Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">Brother of Vasantrao, named on the About page as co-founder.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Successor</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Vasudeva V. Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Son of Vasantrao. Consolidated the industrial activities. A former trustee of
              the Dempo Charities Trust, and one of the founders who supported Fr Romualdo
              D’Souza in starting the Goa Institute of Management.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Media and trusts</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Pallavi S. Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Wife of the chairman. MBA from Pune University. Handles the media businesses
              and the charitable trusts. Joined the gift toward the Tepper Quad Building.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Charities Trust</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Rajesh R. Bhatikar</h3>
            <p class="muted">Administrator, Dempo Charities Trust, signatory of the 2026 scholarship scheme.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Human resources</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Arvind Kuri</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Named as Dempo Group HR Head in the September 2025 report on support for
              Niklesh Pednekar. The careers page asks applicants to write to the General
              Manager, Human Resources. The homepage asks for the Senior General Manager,
              Human Resources. A September 2024 sponsorship note names Dr. Krishna Gopal
              Rajanala as General Manager, HR. Those titles are left as published.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Chairman’s office</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Girija Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              The 9 September 2025 report of a Dempo Vishwa Gramshala school visit names her
              Executive Assistant to the Chairman. No wider biography is published.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Anniversary</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Yatish Dempo</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Attended the 4 March 2024 founder anniversary at the head office, with Pallavi
              Dempo. The post gives him no title. [Placeholder: client to confirm]
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Goa Carbon, 2024</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Anupam Misra</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Named executive director of Goa Carbon at the June 2024 launch of gcarb+. The
              site does not publish a current board list.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="row-index">Finance, 2024</span>
            <h3 class="row-title">Sharmila Prabhu</h3>
            <p class="muted">
              Senior General Manager, Finance and Taxation, in the September 2024 note on
              sponsorship for swimmer Aarohi Borde. Present with Dr. Krishna Gopal Rajanala.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 2rem">
        <span class="tag">[Placeholder: client to supply]</span>
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        A current board, executive committee and company-wise leadership list is not
        published as a single page on dempos.com. This concept does not invent one.
        Photographs of Pallavi S. Dempo and of the wider leadership are also not supplied here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
